<main>

<p>This policy explains what this app does with your information. It is published in English and applies to the app whichever language you read it in.</p>

<p>In short: you do not need an account, nothing you type is sent to us, and the only information that leaves your device goes to Google for showing ads and for basic app stability reporting.</p>

<h2>App covered by this policy</h2>

<!-- Replace the app name and package ID below with the exact values from your Play Console listing. -->
<ul class="apps">
  <li>Marathi Calendar &amp; Panchang<span class="pkg">com.dipali.marathicalendar</span></li>
</ul>

<p>This app's Google Play listing links to this page. If an app is not named here, this policy does not cover it.</p>

<h2>Information the app collects</h2>

<h3>Information you provide</h3>
<p>None. The app does not ask you to register, sign in, or give a name, email address or phone number. Your settings — the city you have chosen, reminders you have set, and similar preferences — are saved on your device and stay there. Uninstalling the app removes them.</p>

<h3>Location</h3>
<p>Panchang timings such as tithi, nakshatra, rahu kaal, sunrise and sunset change with where you are, so the app needs a location to calculate them. You choose a city from the built-in list, and the app keeps that choice on your device. If the app offers to detect your location instead, it only does so after you grant Android's location permission, and it uses the result to select the nearest city. Your location is used for these calculations and is not stored on any server run by us.</p>
<p>You can withdraw location permission at any time in Android Settings, under Apps, then the app, then Permissions. The app keeps working — you pick your city by hand.</p>
<p>Separately, Google's advertising services may estimate an approximate location from your IP address. This is described below.</p>

<h3>Advertising and diagnostic information</h3>
<p>The app shows advertisements supplied by Google AdMob, and uses Google Play services. Through these, Google may collect and process:</p>
<ul>
  <li>your device's advertising ID and other device or app identifiers;</li>
  <li>your IP address, and an approximate location derived from it;</li>
  <li>device details such as model, operating system version, language and screen size;</li>
  <li>information about how ads were served and interacted with;</li>
  <li>crash reports and basic stability diagnostics, so problems in the app can be found and fixed.</li>
</ul>
<p>We receive this only as aggregated reporting — counts and totals that do not identify you. We never see the contents of your device, your contacts, your files or your messages.</p>

<h2>Advertising</h2>

<p>Ads pay for the app, which is why it is free. They are served by Google AdMob, whose handling of data is described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a> and in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<p>Depending on where you are and what you have agreed to, ads may be personalised — chosen using your advertising ID and past activity — or non-personalised, chosen only from the app's context. If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, the app shows a consent screen the first time it runs, where you can accept or refuse personalised ads. You can reopen that screen from the app's settings and change your answer.</p>

<p>Anywhere in the world, you can limit ad personalisation from your device: open Android Settings, then Privacy or Google, then Ads, and choose to delete or reset your advertising ID. You will still see ads, but they will not be based on your advertising ID.</p>

<h2>Sharing</h2>

<p>We do not sell your information, and we do not share it with anyone for their own marketing. Information is shared only with Google, in its role as our advertising and app-services provider, in the ways described above. We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to investigate fraud or a security problem.</p>

<h2>Permissions the app asks for</h2>

<ul class="perm">
  <li><b>Internet and network state</b> — needed to load ads and to download updated calendar and festival data.</li>
  <li><b>Location (optional)</b> — used only to pick the nearest city for timing calculations. Refusing it does not limit the app.</li>
  <li><b>Notifications (optional)</b> — used to remind you about a tithi, festival or fasting day you have asked to be reminded of. Reminders are generated on your device.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Accuracy of calendar information</h2>

<p>Panchang, festival and holiday dates are provided for your convenience and are calculated from publicly available astronomical and calendrical data. Regional traditions differ, and dates may vary between panchang systems. The app is an independent work and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to any published almanac, panchang brand or government body.</p>

<h2>How long information is kept</h2>

<p>Settings and preferences stay on your device until you clear the app's data or uninstall it. Information held by Google is kept according to Google's own retention policies, which are set out in the Google Privacy Policy linked above.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>

<p>Data sent between the app and Google's services is encrypted in transit. Because the app does not run an account system or a server that stores your personal information, there is no database of users to be lost or stolen. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so absolute security cannot be promised.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>

<p>This app is made for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through this app, write to the address below and it will be deleted.</p>

<h2>Your rights and choices</h2>

<p>You can reset or delete your advertising ID, withdraw location permission, change your ad-personalisation consent, or uninstall the app — each of these takes effect immediately and none of them requires our involvement.</p>

<p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, you have rights of access, correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability over personal data relating to you. If you are in India, the Digital Personal Data Protection Act gives you comparable rights. Because we hold no account or profile about you, most of these requests are best directed to Google, which processes the advertising data. For anything within our control, write to the address below and you will get a reply within 30 days.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

<p>This page is updated when the app changes or when the law requires it. The effective date at the top shows when the current version took effect. Significant changes will be noted in the app's release notes on Google Play.</p>

